  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>It is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised&nbsp;low spin complex as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is a strong field ligand.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>II</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>RuCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Low spin complex as Ru belongs to 4d series, as elements belonging to 4d and 5d series forms low spin complexes even with weak field ligand.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ru</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Kr</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;set contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>Its configuration is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></math></p><p>It has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is weak field ligand.</p><p>So, its Magnetic moment,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>IV</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></p><p>It has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>, its&nbsp;Magnetic moment,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
